      "description": "Reference to video on Sulphur 3. Sulphur 3 is SulphurAI's uncensored finetune of MiniMax H3, trained on the FL2VA base. This card loads the author's 11.4 GB W4A8 file, the one their own example workflow uses.\n\nA five-second 480p shot takes about 2 3/4 minutes on a 12 GB card in the app.\n\nSupply reference pictures of the same person. The reference never appears in the video, so the prompt must describe the whole shot. The author also publishes a separate reference variant marked as not yet trained; this card uses the main model. Reference video and audio inputs are untested.\n\nIt runs the author's settings: Euler with the simple schedule, 20 steps, CFG 1. The model is guidance-distilled, so a negative prompt does nothing. The Steps control goes from 12 to 30, but only 20 was tested.\n\nThe author prompts with JSON captions written by their own prompt tool. In our test a JSON version of the same prompt changed little apart from louder sound, so the usual three-field H3 prompt works.\n\nNot included: the author's optional corrector, which needs extra nodes and about 8 GB more video memory. W4A8 keeps the weights in 4 bits; there is no int8 file of this model yet to compare it with. No LoRAs were tested.\n\nAn 11.4 GB download of its own, separate from the 10Eros packs.\n\nModel format: W4A8 (4-bit weights, group size 16) with ConvRot.",
